{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/890725-2e-arrows-mysteries","id":890725,"title":"[2E] Arrows Mysteries?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-14T12:49:37-07:00","id":890725,"title":"[2E] Arrows Mysteries?","content":"I remember from development phase when there was comment by the <b>DaveB</b> ( I so pose ) that stated that Arrows can take non-magical Obsessions based on service for other mages and their Oaths. However, all I could find in new corebook is this quote. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adamantine Arrow write-up</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mysteries</b><br /> Arrows look for Mysteries that threaten their charges, seeking to understand malicious magic with superior knowledge and craft intent to better end the threat. They seek to aid other Diamond Orders in the often-perilous experience of investigating their own Mysteries. Alternately, an Arrow will swear oaths to uncover a secret, proving dominance with self-mastery by pitting herself against a singular foe. An attractive Mystery for an Arrow involves a test or contest of his skill; Arrows are disappointed when the Fallen World gives up its secrets too easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did I missed something? Arrows cannot take Oaths ( or similar dedications ) as their Obsessions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T13:49:44-07:00","id":890767,"title":"","content":"I think a non-magical Obsession for an Arrow mage is simply just a potent Aspiration, seeing as Obsessions grant Arcane Experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T15:41:11-07:00","id":890842,"title":"","content":"If they're studying a magically enforced Oath then it would probably be solid ground for an Obsession. I don't think it counts if it's an Oath they've made themselves though since there's no mystery there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T15:49:19-07:00","id":890845,"title":"","content":"Yeah, an Arrow's Oath is grounds for an Obsession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T20:04:18-07:00","id":890936,"title":"","content":"So if, let's say, Banner Warden is making Oath to protect his cabal, he can write &quot;Protecting cabal&quot; as Obsession and generate Arcane Beats from this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T17:47:45-07:00","id":891476,"title":"","content":"I'd say something like &quot;study and understand the effects of a service oath on destiny and sympathy&quot; would work. Or even try removing the oath, and just say &quot;understand how being in service to another mage furthers my destiny and wisdom&quot;. i dunno if the last one is too broad, as itd allow wisdom and regular obsessive gains. But I'd lean in that direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T18:15:09-07:00","id":891486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/890725-2e-arrows-mysteries?p=890936#post890936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if, let's say, Banner Warden is making Oath to protect his cabal, he can write &quot;Protecting cabal&quot; as Obsession and generate Arcane Beats from this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Be careful, they are going to be penalized when provoking degeneration checks related to their Oath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T20:36:55-07:00","id":891550,"title":"","content":"From Dave's post it would seem that making an Oath and then pursuing it is enough to be an Obsession for an Arrow. Which makes sense, following an Oath to its conclusion in disregard for any of the consequences fits the Arrow pretty well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T20:45:51-07:00","id":891552,"title":"","content":"I feel that my Arrow player would object heavily if I penalized her Wisdom roll for protecting her Cabal, but I can certainly see interesting implications here. Horror game and stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T21:06:18-07:00","id":891559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/890725-2e-arrows-mysteries?p=891552#post891552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that my Arrow player would object heavily if I penalized her Wisdom roll for protecting her Cabal, but I can certainly see interesting implications here. Horror game and stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they consider their Cabal's safety so important that they're willing to commit acts of Hubris to protect it, taking a penalty to their Wisdom roll seems quite appropriate, especially for an Arrow. It puts the focus on the ethics of their conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T21:14:05-07:00","id":891563,"title":"","content":"Most people would expect that protecting your sacred Oath would have an effect closer to Virtue (roll extra dice) than an Obsession (lose one rolled dice). I can see benefit of both approaches.<br /> ...I wonder if a character with multiple Virtues can get multiple dice to Wisdom roll. That would finally give some meat for these extra-Virtue and extra-Vice merits from core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T21:31:39-07:00","id":891574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/890725-2e-arrows-mysteries?p=891563#post891563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most people would expect that protecting your sacred Oath would have an effect closer to Virtue (roll extra dice) than an Obsession (lose one rolled dice). I can see benefit of both approaches..</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that this works as both - it is both Virtue-like and Obsession - so both +1 and -1 to Wisdom check. Remember, player still decided to make &quot;protecting cabal&quot; source of his magical studies. And it's still more beneficiary for the Arrow than normal pursuing Obsession, as it then only -1 penalty, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T08:09:39-07:00","id":987754,"title":"","content":"How are Arrow Oaths handled mechanically in 2ed? So far, I can see how they work into obsessions, but if you have the Oathbound Merit from the AA book, how would that now translate? <br /> <br /> Another question regarding the Oathbound Merit; If the merit can still apply in 2ed, are the three oaths listed in the AA book (Allegiance, Principle, and Questing) the only oaths Arrows are able to make? If there are other oaths, what kind of mechanical benefits would I be able to provide to the players in game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11310-phoenixfallen","name":"Phoenixfallen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T08:55:37-07:00","id":987775,"title":"","content":"I don't think that Mages are limited to having only one Oath on their Pattern anymore, so you don't really need the Oathbound merit for that. The other effects can probably just be covered by the Oath spell using Reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 10-15-2016, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T07:22:36-07:00","id":988239,"title":"","content":"Prior to 2nd Edition, I played an Acanthus Arrow who was also a member of the House of Ariadne. This game's Mystery revolved around the city of Cleveland and exploring why it was such a hellhole: because an archmage created a time and space twisting, mind bending, Abyssal labyrinth beneath the city! Anyways...<br /> <br /> All the Arrows arrive in the city and meetup with the Adamant Sage and his two lieutenants and they take an Oath to them. It's your standard chain of command type of thing. Arrows were in Cleveland in order to protect the mages who were investigation the Labyrinth. My character was also there to find missing members of her Legacy who had come to explore from Chicago. A big element of the story was that many mages had gone to Cleveland, never to be heard from again.<br /> <br /> Being an Acanthus and an Arrow, my character (Jude) had a personality quirk that eventually led to a lot of great interpersonal conflict. She always kept her word, and she never made a promise she couldn't keep. This manifested as a sort of flighty, or roguish attitude in that Jude really didn't say anything that could commit her to action or loyalty or anything unless she was absolutely sure she could keep her word. This created a sort of persona for her as someone who could be trusted because everyone learned that Jude would do anything to keep her word. If she told she would do something, no matter how difficult or foolish, <i>she absolutely would do it.</i> Being a member of the House of Ariadne, she walked around boasting, &quot;I can find anything...&quot; and people would contract her to help them find things. If she agreed to help you, it was as good as saying, &quot;You've won! Whatever you lost will be found soon.&quot;<br /> <br /> That kind of thing in 2nd Edition would be an Obsession, right?<br /> <br /> Her penchant for never breaking her word lead to conflict when the Adamant Sage and his lieutenants were discovered to be tainted by the Abyss... We weren't even sure if they were human anymore, or if they ever were! Did we all come to Cleveland and swear our allegiance to Gulmoth in human form? Were we tricked? Stuff like that. Things came to a head when the mages of the city banded together and attempted to kill these imposters (?) ... meanwhile Jude and some other mages were on another mission: to actually break into Arrow's headquarters and find evidence/proof of this Abyssal taint. When the Adamant Sage was deposed, a member of Jude's cabal stepped up and took the mantle of Adamant Sage, declaring himself leader of the Arrows and he asked that all the other Arrows in the city swear their loyalty to him. Jude refused because she had already made that promise to the former Adamant Sage and his lieutenants. Until they released her form her Oath or they died, she would not divide her loyalties. This cemented Jude's status as a Wild Card or Loose Cannon -- I preferred the term Black Swan -- and created some of the best roleplay ever!<br /> <br /> That's an Obsession, right?<br /> <br /> Also, would following the path Fate lays out for you regardless of consequences be an Obsession? An example is: Jude's Arrow mentor was one of these tainted lieutenants. She was captured and Jude went to interrogate her. Great scene and all that... and she even taught Jude Spirit magic so she could commune with the spirits (Abyssal and otherwise) in the City, so that Jude could do her duty and save the City. In the end, her mentor asked to be executed and Jude wouldn't make that decision. She left it in the hands of Fate. Her signature weapon was a six-shooter revolver. Jude removed three of the bullets from the cylinder and spun it. She put the barrel to her mentors head and pulled the trigger. I rolled 1 die... Odds, the gun clicks, Even, BOOM! It was even... and one of the highest ranking mages in the city was murdered in cold blood.<br /> <br /> That's an Obsession, right? Like Two-Face from Batman, huh?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T11:56:14-07:00","id":988324,"title":"","content":"Those seem like they would be Obsessions and acts orienting around Obsessions, yeah.<br /> <br /> I liked the Adamantine Arrow book, I'm guessing you read it. The idea that they believe their code of honor is not just for them, but them attempting to concrete their belief of the Supernal and how the Fallen World should be actually onto the world, through their actions, was a great hook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:44:48-07:00","id":988415,"title":"","content":"I don't recall reading anything that would preclude an Obsession that happens to align perfectly with a virtue. That would mean both applied regularly.<br /> <br /> Unless I'm missing something, that's all already handled by stacking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}